.TH T3-AUTH-PROXY 1
.SH NAME
t3-auth-proxy \- manage a shared T3 Code session behind an SSO gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B t3-auth-proxy
[\fB-config\fR FILE] [\fB-force\fR] serve|ensure-token|status
.br
.B t3-auth-proxy -version
.SH DESCRIPTION
The proxy authenticates upstream requests with a T3 Code bearer session issued
by the local t3 CLI. HTTP, streamed responses and WebSocket upgrades are forwarded
using Go's standard reverse proxy. This program does not implement an SSO login.
Only trusted ingress addresses may reach it; every allowed peer must enforce
authentication before forwarding requests. Do not expose its port directly.
.PP
All clients share one T3 identity and its default full-access permissions.
Revoke user access at the SSO gateway. Existing WebSockets are not automatically
closed when a gateway login is revoked. Local users who can reach an allowed
loopback listener also have access.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Validate or issue a session, then listen. Reload the state file every two seconds.
An expired token fails closed with HTTP 503. Upstream failures return HTTP 502.
.TP
.B ensure-token
Check the current session against T3. Issue and validate a replacement when
revoked, expired or inside the renewal window. The -force option rotates early.
Writes are atomic and a file lock prevents concurrent issuance. A failed
candidate leaves the previous token intact. Retired sessions remain usable
until expiry; expired sessions tracked by this program are revoked on rotation.
.TP
.B status
Print version, session ID, expiry and authentication status as JSON, never the token.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration is /etc/t3-auth-proxy.conf, in JSON format.
An example is installed alongside it; installation never overwrites configuration.
.TP
.B listen
Listener address. Default: 127.0.0.1:3773.
.TP
.B upstream
T3 HTTP origin. Default: http://127.0.0.1:3774. Keep this listener private.
.TP
.B public_url
Required public HTTP(S) origin. Used for Host, forwarded headers and Origin checks.
Requests carrying a different Origin are rejected.
.TP
.B trusted_peers
CIDRs allowed to reach the proxy. Defaults to IPv4 and IPv6 loopback.
Set these to the actual gateway or tunnel connector addresses, not client addresses.
.TP
.B t3_binary, t3_home
The t3 executable (default: t3 on PATH) and optional T3 home passed as --base-dir.
Use an absolute executable path for systemd.
.TP
.B state_dir
State directory. Defaults to STATE_DIRECTORY from systemd, otherwise
/var/lib/t3-auth-proxy. Contains session.json and renew.lock. Keep it private.
.TP
.B token_ttl, renew_before
Go duration strings. Defaults: 720h (30 days) and 168h (7 days).
The CLI's pairing-code lifetime is unrelated to these settings.
.TP
.B subject
Label and subject for sessions created by this proxy. Default: t3-auth-proxy.
.SH INSTALLATION
Install the release binary, man page and systemd units with make install.
Create /etc/t3-auth-proxy.conf from the example and configure T3 to listen on
the private upstream address. Use the same Linux user as the T3 installation:
.PP
.nf
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable --now t3-auth-proxy@USER.service
systemctl enable --now t3-auth-proxy-renew@USER.timer
.fi
.PP
The units create /var/lib/t3-auth-proxy-USER with owner-only access. The T3
daemon must already be configured to start at boot. The proxy retries startup
if T3 is not ready. Do not run multiple proxy instances with the same config.
.SH OPERATIONS
Use systemctl status and journalctl -u t3-auth-proxy@USER.service for service logs.
Run status as USER with STATE_DIRECTORY set to the unit's state directory.
Run the renew service manually to check credentials immediately.
.PP
Rotation changes new requests without restarting T3 or the proxy. Existing
sockets retain their old session and may reconnect when it expires. The proxy
does not replay failed requests, especially writes. If the gateway login expires,
sign in again at the gateway.
.PP
T3 session cookies, DPoP headers and wsTicket/dpop query credentials are removed
before forwarding so stale browser credentials cannot override the shared token.
Other cookies and query parameters are preserved. The proxy does not store or
log request bodies or authentication tokens. Tested against T3 Code 0.1.9.
.SH UPGRADES
Install a new release binary and restart the proxy. Preserve its configuration
and state directory. Test HTTP, WebSockets and token issuance after T3 upgrades.
To revert to native pairing, stop the proxy and restore the previous T3 listener
and gateway target. Revoke the proxy's sessions when retiring the deployment.
.SH FILES
/usr/local/bin/t3-auth-proxy
.br
/etc/t3-auth-proxy.conf
.br
/var/lib/t3-auth-proxy-USER/session.json
.br
/usr/local/lib/systemd/system/t3-auth-proxy*.service
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; one on configuration, issuance or runtime failure.
